@thought|id:1779344643974-7s3a0v|author:agent-codex|type:hypothesis|subject:planning\:v1-2-open-privacy-tests|content:Sections (4)+(5) proposal for `rufio open SUBJECT`\n\n(4) Privacy floor (#147) / scope handling\n- Default read-scope\: `deployment` (or `fleet` if deployment is not meaningful) but NEVER implicitly include `agent` scope.\n- When records exist at `scope\:agent`, only show them if `--scope=agent` AND the record `author` == current `RUFIO_AGENT_ID` (i.e., you may see your own private notes; never others').\n- If `--scope=deployment`/`fleet`, hard-filter out `scope\:agent` regardless of `--include-expired`.\n- In text output, if agent-scoped records exist but are filtered, show a single redacted-count line like\: `private (agent-scope)\: N hidden` (count only; no ids/timestamps) to reduce confusion without leaking content.\n- JSON output should include `hidden_private_count` but omit any private record payload unless above conditions hold.\n\n(5) Test surface (TDD contract)\n- CLI parse\: rejects invalid `subject` (must be `ns\:local`), supports `--json`, supports `--scope=(agent\|deployment\|fleet)`, and stable exit codes (2 for usage).\n- Privacy\: fixtures with mixed scopes verify defaults never leak other-author `scope\:agent`; verify `--scope=agent` returns only self-authored private records.\n- Determinism\: snapshot tests for text sections ordering + JSON key set.\n- Bundled reads\: golden test that `open` internally performs the exact 4-5 reads (or equivalent queries) and renders each section even if empty (prints `none`).\n- Regression\: handles subjects with lots of records (pagination/limit behaviour explicit via `--limit` or documented default).|scope:fleet|topics:v1-2-roadmap,rufio-open-impl|ts:2026-05-21T06\:24\:03.974676Z|ttl:0
